From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6prm: handle GPR_BASIC_RSP_RESULT

The SM6115 ADSP firmware can answer a PRM command with a GPR basic
response instead of the PRM response opcode. q6prm ignores it, so the
sender waits for the full timeout. Record the reported opcode and status
and wake the waiter, as q6apm does, so a DSP error is returned as one.
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6prm.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6prm.c
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6prm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6prm.c
@@ -190,6 +190,12 @@
 		prm->result.status = result->status;
 		wake_up(&prm->wait);
 		break;
+	case GPR_BASIC_RSP_RESULT:
+		result = data->payload;
+		prm->result.opcode = result->opcode;
+		prm->result.status = result->status;
+		wake_up(&prm->wait);
+		break;
 	default:
 		break;
 	}

